      "en": "Asking a non-Jew to perform a melacha on Shabbat is rabbinically forbidden under 'Amirah LeNochri Shevut', even through hints. Furthermore, one cannot benefit from melacha done specifically for a Jew until 'bichdei sheya'asu' (the time it takes to do it) after Shabbat. However, an exception is permitted for a 'choleh she'ein bo sakanah' (someone ill without life danger) or in conditions of extreme cold (mitztate'ar).",
