      "en": "'Kavod Shabbat' relates to actions performed in honor of the incoming holy day before it begins, such as bathing, cleaning the home, setting the table, and donning fine clothes. 'Oneg Shabbat' refers to experiencing delight on Shabbat itself, fulfilled through three festive meals featuring delicious food and wine, joyful singing of zemirot, Torah study, and restful sleep. Both obligations are derived from the verse in Isaiah: 'And you shall call the Sabbath a delight, the holy day of Hashem honorable.'",
