      "en": "Orlah is a biblical prohibition forbidding any eating or deriving of benefit from fruit grown during the first three years of a fruit tree's planting, applying both in Israel and by Halacha LeMoshe MiSinai abroad. In the fourth year, the fruit has the status of Neta Revai: in ancient times it was eaten with sanctity in Jerusalem, but today its holiness must be redeemed onto a coin worth at least a Perutah before it can be eaten. One must ensure that purchased fruits, or those picked from private trees, are certified as having passed the Orlah years.",
