      "en": "Both the Written Torah (Tanach) and the Oral Torah were revealed by Hashem to Moshe Rabbeinu at Mount Sinai, as the written text cannot be understood or observed without its divine oral explanation. This sacred tradition was codified over generations: Rabbi Yehuda HaNasi redacted the Mishnah, Ravina and Rav Ashi compiled the Gemara (Talmud Bavli), the Rambam synthesized practical Halacha in the Mishneh Torah, and Maran Rav Yosef Karo compiled the definitive Shulchan Aruch, supplemented by the Rema's Ashkenazi glosses (the Mapah). Today, authentic Orthodox practice relies directly on this unbroken chain of Mesorah.",
