      "en": "In Halacha, performing a pious custom three consecutive times without stipulating otherwise endows it with the halachic status of a binding vow (Neder). If a woman later misses it due to illness or household fatigue, she risks violating a serious Torah prohibition of breaking a vow unless she undergoes Hatarat Nedarim. Therefore, whenever taking on an extra spiritual practice—like reciting Shir HaShirim or giving specific Tzedakah—one must explicitly declare 'Bli Neder' to preserve flexibility.",
